[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335824096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109009#issuecomment-3335824096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109009","id":3335824096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G1KLg","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T20:26:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T20:26:25Z","body":"Thoughts of creating the godot physics version of tapered capsules? I've been trying to avoid porting the tapered capsule physics algorithm due to complexity and doing a convex hull seems complicated too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3335824096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3417323003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109009#issuecomment-3417323003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109009","id":3417323003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LsDX7","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T21:40:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T21:40:49Z","body":"I like that this allows us to implement the proposed KHR physics extensions for glTF. There was positive feedback in the animation meeting about the new shape.\r\n\r\nOriginally, I was hoping we could add functionality to the existing capsule shape to extend radius to be the mid-radius, and a taper property. The internal Jolt type is still SHAPE_CAPSULE. The problem @fire explained is we need to use mid_height instead of height, since the meaning of height as the outer height depends on the combined upper and lower radii. This explains why creating a new tapered collision shape is perhaps the most prudent choice, but I'd be interested to see if others have ideas on keeping one capsule type while still maintaining compatibility.\r\n\r\nMost importantly, we need someone deeply involved in physics to also give this a look over.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3417323003/reactions","to